From: baseband lane
Subject: 0548 pandora_adsp: the QRTR experiment attaches on the ADSP edge, not on whichever agrees first

gl_report() runs once per edge, and 0547 put the one-shot qrtr_tried guard in it without asking which
edge it was looking at.  There are two edges (ed_adsp "ADSP" and ed_soccp "SOCCP"), and the first one to
agree a GLINK version would have taken the single attempt -- on this phone that is not guaranteed to be
the ADSP, and attaching the QRTR client to the SOCCP's link would have exercised it against the wrong
peer and told the wrong story.

The condition now also requires e == &ed_adsp.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/pandora_adsp.c b/b/bsd/dev/pandora_adsp.c
index e298a81..7ccd2fe 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/pandora_adsp.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/pandora_adsp.c
@@ -1526,7 +1526,7 @@ gl_report(struct edge *e, bool force)
 		static bool qrtr_tried;
 		uint32_t on = 0;
 
-		if (!qrtr_tried && e->gl.version_agreed &&
+		if (!qrtr_tried && e == &ed_adsp && e->gl.version_agreed &&
 		    PE_parse_boot_argn("pandora_adsp_qrtr", &on, sizeof(on)) && on == 1) {
 			qrtr_tried = true;
 			(void)pandora_qrtr_attach(&e->gl, "IPCRTR");
